  "question": {
    "text": "Which of the following expressions corresponds to simple harmonic motion along a straight line, where $x$ is the displacement and $a, b, c$ are positive constants?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "gZKSo",
      "text": "$a+b x-c x^{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SPGCD",
      "text": "$b x^{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "x3m4M",
      "text": "$a-b x+c x^{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1Nxft",
      "text": "$-b x$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "In linear S.H.M., the restoring force acting on particle should always be proportional to the displacement of the particle and directed towards the equilibrium position. i.e., $\\mathrm{F} \\propto \\mathrm{x}$\nor $\\mathrm{F}=-\\mathrm{bx}$ where $\\mathrm{b}$ is a positive constant.",
    "image": null
  },
